s (playing 99 or JJ), where your hand is structurally superior, or simply play out your high cards backed by the Rocket and 22. Passing is passive and unnecessary given your hand strength, and playing a 2 breaks a valuable pair.\n\nReason: The single Ace beats the King efficiently without breaking the powerful pair of 2s or the Rocket. Gaining the lead allows the Landlord to dictate the game flow, likely switching to pairs (99, JJ) to clear the hand quickly while holding the Rocket and 22 as invincible backup.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣A"]}'}
